WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.399 --> 00:00:05.540
Superhero movies are chock full of high-flying
action, shocking moments, and lately, plenty

00:00:05.540 --> 00:00:06.540
of humor.

00:00:06.540 --> 00:00:10.440
But for all the jokes that actually make it
into the final cut, there are plenty more

00:00:10.440 --> 00:00:12.530
that remain on the cutting room floor.

00:00:12.530 --> 00:00:16.740
Thankfully, there's the blooper reel, the
time-honored tradition of capturing those

00:00:16.740 --> 00:00:19.779
moments when actors goof off or screw up.

00:00:19.779 --> 00:00:24.410
From comic book references to slick dance
moves, here are bloopers that will make you

00:00:24.410 --> 00:00:27.519
love superhero movies even more.

00:00:27.519 --> 00:00:29.089
Blooper-sense tingling

00:00:29.089 --> 00:00:33.910
With Spider-Man: Homecoming, Tom Holland gave
audiences the third live-action Spider-Man

00:00:33.910 --> 00:00:35.660
franchise in 15 years.

00:00:35.660 --> 00:00:40.340
Considering how familiar audiences were with
the character, the filmmakers wisely veered

00:00:40.340 --> 00:00:43.350
away from dwelling on the web-head's origin
story.

00:00:43.350 --> 00:00:47.520
Still, that didn't stop Holland from putting
a reference in the blooper reel.

00:00:47.520 --> 00:00:51.960
When Peter Parker attempts to tell a teacher
why he can't commit any more time to a school

00:00:51.960 --> 00:00:57.370
activity because of his involvement with Tony
Stark, Holland makes a clever callback to

00:00:57.370 --> 00:00:59.820
one of the most famous lines in Spider-Man
history:

00:00:59.820 --> 00:01:04.280
"I got a lot of responsibility with it.

00:01:04.280 --> 00:01:06.930
With great power comes great responsibility."

00:01:06.930 --> 00:01:10.390
With great power comes great comic book knowledge.

00:01:10.390 --> 00:01:12.420
Super movies need super glue

00:01:12.420 --> 00:01:18.680
Black Panther stars Chadwick Boseman as king
T'Challa, the titular Black Panther, a hero

00:01:18.680 --> 00:01:22.920
empowered by the Heart-Shaped Herb and a connection
to the spiritual realm.

00:01:22.920 --> 00:01:28.070
The movie, meanwhile, was empowered by a script
that was just as much about a fascinating

00:01:28.070 --> 00:01:31.380
villain, Michael B. Jordan's Erik Killmonger.

00:01:31.760 --> 00:01:33.600
"I want the throne."

00:01:34.040 --> 00:01:38.440
Still, regardless of how deep the characters
are, action movies need stuff to get blown

00:01:38.440 --> 00:01:39.440
up.

00:01:39.440 --> 00:01:44.030
In one scene, it's up to Killmonger to attach
some explosives to a building, but the blooper

00:01:44.030 --> 00:01:47.320
reel reveals that it definitely took a few
tries.

00:01:53.440 --> 00:01:56.980
You'd think Marvel could afford better prop
glue.

00:01:56.990 --> 00:01:58.479
Strange things are afoot

00:01:58.479 --> 00:02:03.840
Doctor Strange is one of the strangest Marvel
Comics properties, and effectively bringing

00:02:03.840 --> 00:02:08.580
the character to the screen required the involvement
of a very serious actor.

00:02:08.580 --> 00:02:13.510
Benedict Cumberbatch ended up being exactly
what the doctor ordered, so to speak, and

00:02:13.510 --> 00:02:19.120
he brings real gravitas to Dr. Stephen Strange
- a guy who can use magic and tap into the

00:02:19.120 --> 00:02:22.720
powers of mystical entities in his fight against
evil.

00:02:22.720 --> 00:02:23.870
"Dr. Strange."

00:02:23.870 --> 00:02:26.019
"Oh, we're using our made-up names.

00:02:26.019 --> 00:02:27.620
Then, I am Spider-Man."

00:02:27.620 --> 00:02:32.779
Still, despite the importance of the actor,
the importance of the character, and the importance

00:02:32.780 --> 00:02:37.720
of his mission, sometimes all Cumberbatch
can do is just dance.

00:02:39.120 --> 00:02:41.700
[Grunting]

00:02:44.120 --> 00:02:45.300
"Yeah!"

00:02:46.260 --> 00:02:51.239
After seeing that, we kind of wish some of
these sweet dance moves had made it into the

00:02:51.239 --> 00:02:52.239
film.

00:02:52.239 --> 00:02:53.349
Thor meets floor

00:02:53.349 --> 00:02:59.620
Thor: Ragnarok, the third entry in the MCU
film franchise about Chris Hemsworth's titular

00:02:59.620 --> 00:03:02.889
Norse deity, mixed up the formula a little
bit.

00:03:02.889 --> 00:03:07.769
Under the direction of Taika Waititi, the
movie is more of a comedy about superheroes

00:03:07.769 --> 00:03:09.999
than a straightforward superhero movie.

00:03:09.999 --> 00:03:14.480
"But if I'm being honest, when it comes to
fighting evil beings, he is very powerful

00:03:14.480 --> 00:03:15.480
and useful."

00:03:15.480 --> 00:03:16.959
"Yeah, Banner's powerful and useful, too."

00:03:16.959 --> 00:03:18.189
"Is he, though?"

00:03:18.189 --> 00:03:22.480
Still, for all the jokes and physical comedy
that made it into the actual movie, there

00:03:22.480 --> 00:03:25.609
were plenty that were relegated to the gag
reel.

00:03:25.609 --> 00:03:30.650
While trying to get out the line, "A wise
king never seeks power," Hemsworth can't walk

00:03:30.650 --> 00:03:34.750
and talk at the same time, and gets stymied
by an errant step.

00:03:34.750 --> 00:03:36.499
"A wise king never seeks power.

00:03:36.499 --> 00:03:37.499
Ah, f---.

00:03:37.499 --> 00:03:40.340
One step, every time that gets me!"

00:03:40.340 --> 00:03:44.950
Seems like the God of Thunder isn't the God
of descending staircases.

00:03:44.950 --> 00:03:46.699
Stormy relationship

00:03:46.699 --> 00:03:52.139
While filming a scene for X-Men: Days of Future
Past, Halle Berry and Hugh Jackman were supposed

00:03:52.139 --> 00:03:55.629
to exchange some soft words and a tender goodbye
kiss.

00:03:55.629 --> 00:03:59.640
"So, basically I'm the only one who's going
to remember any of this, right?"

00:03:59.640 --> 00:04:00.260
"I think so."

00:04:02.680 --> 00:04:04.500
"Okay then."

00:04:05.000 --> 00:04:09.520
Berry's obviously been waiting for this moment
for a really long time.

00:04:09.520 --> 00:04:10.980
"See you later."

00:04:13.280 --> 00:04:17.100
[Screaming and laughing]

00:04:17.760 --> 00:04:18.760
Thanks for watching!

00:04:18.760 --> 00:04:21.780
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:04:21.780 --> 00:04:24.699
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

